  "prefLabel": "Plc 602.13 Infectious waste",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 602.13 “Infectious waste” means any:\n\n(a) Liquid or semi-liquid blood;\n\n(b) Items contaminated with blood that could release the blood in a liquid or semi-liquid state if compressed;\n\n(c) Items that are caked with dried blood and are capable of releasing the blood during handling; or\n\n(d) Sharps that have been used or are otherwise contaminated.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Plc 600) #12622, eff 9-21-18 (formerly Plc 401.02); ss by #14631, eff 9-21-26, EXPIRES: 9-21-36 (formerly Plc 601.02)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc600.html"
